    {
      "id": "O4",
      "area": "Child clarity and visual hierarchy",
      "observation": "The ink/navy Child library has clear Library/Ask Parent navigation and visible Daily time \u00b7 1 min left. Exhausted copy explains 7 AM renewal; Parent-stopped copy instead says Parent will let the child know. Both retain Choose profile. Text is readable and calm. Countdown library layouts adapt from phone two-column cards to tablet/desktop grids. Synthetic blank video thumbnails cannot substantiate media appeal.",
